        "active_lock_reason": null,
        "body": "### Description\n\nThe PATCH endpoint for messages reports incorrect Retry-After if a message is crossposted.\r\n\r\nThe response is a code 429 with the headers:\r\n\r\n```\r\n< retry-after: 1\r\n< x-ratelimit-scope: shared\r\n< x-ratelimit-bucket: 1d3c67957bcdccc6709861c232df8529\r\n< x-ratelimit-limit: 5\r\n< x-ratelimit-remaining: 4\r\n< x-ratelimit-reset: 1682258040.904\r\n< x-ratelimit-reset-after: 0.999\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe response body has the correct limit:\r\n\r\n```\r\n{\r\n  \"code\": 20028,\r\n  \"global\": false,\r\n  \"message\": \"The write action you are performing on the channel has hit the write rate limit.\",\r\n  \"retry_after\": 1163.097\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis issue seems to be limited to crossposted messages. Some more detailed logs:\r\n\r\n```\r\nEncountered 429 on route PATCH/channels/{channel_id}/messages/{message_id} with bucket 1d3c67957bcdccc6709861c232df8529:channel_id=702491600693231687 Retry-After: 4000 ms Scope: shared\r\nBacking off 3999 ms for bucket 1d3c67957bcdccc6709861c232df8529:channel_id=702491600693231687 on route PATCH/channels/{channel_id}/messages/{message_id}\r\nEncountered 429 on route PATCH/channels/{channel_id}/messages/{message_id} with bucket 1d3c67957bcdccc6709861c232df8529:channel_id=702491600693231687 Retry-After: 1000 ms Scope: shared\r\nBacking off 1000 ms for bucket 1d3c67957bcdccc6709861c232df8529:channel_id=702491600693231687 on route PATCH/channels/{channel_id}/messages/{message_id}\r\nEncountered 429 on route PATCH/channels/{channel_id}/messages/{message_id} with bucket 1d3c67957bcdccc6709861c232df8529:channel_id=702491600693231687 Retry-After: 1000 ms Scope: shared\r\nBacking off 1000 ms for bucket 1d3c67957bcdccc6709861c232df8529:channel_id=702491600693231687 on route PATCH/channels/{channel_id}/messages/{message_id}\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis retry-loop results in a quick cloudflare API ban.\n\n### Steps to Reproduce\n\n1. Send a message to an announcement channel\r\n2. Crosspost the message\r\n3. Edit it 3 times\r\n\r\nTested using this curl command:\r\n\r\n```\r\ncurl -v \\\r\n-H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\r\n-H \"Authorization: Bot $TOKEN\" \\\r\n-d '{\"content\": \"test edit 4\"}' \\\r\n-X PATCH https://discord.com/api/v10/channels/$channel_id/messages/$message_id\r\n```\n\n### Expected Behavior\n\nThe headers should report the correct rate-limit.\n\n### Current Behavior\n\nThe rate-limit is wrong in the headers.\n\n### Screenshots/Videos\n\n_No response_\n\n### Client and System Information\n\nAPI v10",
