        "author_association": "NONE",
        "active_lock_reason": null,
        "body": "### Description\n\nSystem messages in threads cannot be deleted at all, even by bots. Very disruptive to conversation flow or threads intended to be read-only archives. Users can stop following a thread and it will not produce a message, but if a moderator removes them it will leave a system message that cannot be removed. This also happens when the thread is renamed. Attempting to use a bot to remove these messages gives a permissions error.\n\n### Steps to Reproduce\n\n1. Create a new public thread\r\n2. Rename the thread, or remove a user from the thread\r\n3. Attempt to remove the system message\n\n### Expected Behavior\n\nSystem messages in threads can be deleted same as everywhere else.\n\n### Current Behavior\n\nSystem messages in threads cannot be deleted.\n\n### Screenshots/Videos\n\n**Neither of these messages can be deleted or hidden in any way.**\r\n\r\n![Untitled](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/114151698/233823583-6789cb78-5c7e-486f-ac20-8fcba0845c64.png)\r\n\n\n### Client and System Information\n\nWin10 Stable 191743",
