        "title": "addNumberOption.setMinValue / setMaxValue accepts commas, overlapping float values",
        "user": {
          "login": "menix1337",
          "id": 17611705,
          "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjE3NjExNzA1",
          "gravatar_id": "",
          "url": "https://api.github.com/users/menix1337",
          "type": "User",
          "site_admin": false
        },
        "labels": [
          {
            "id": 2584347154,
            "node_id": "MDU6TGFiZWwyNTg0MzQ3MTU0",
            "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/discord/discord-api-docs/labels/slash%20commands",
            "name": "slash commands",
            "color": "8931af",
            "default": false,
            "description": ""
          }
        ],
        "state": "open",
        "locked": false,
        "assignee": null,
        "assignees": [],
        "milestone": null,
        "comments": 4,
        "created_at": "2023-04-22T11:56:02Z",
        "updated_at": "2023-04-24T23:28:26Z",
        "closed_at": null,
        "author_association": "NONE",
        "active_lock_reason": null,
        "body": "### Description\r\n\r\nUsing float values in addNumberOptions can lead into misleading acceptance of commands, leading into the client thinking values such as 0,1.0 or 0,1 is accepted for the field.\r\n\r\nThe command allows a `,` comma input into the field leaving the field accepting values such as `0,1` erroring out a return as `1.0`\r\n\r\nSo once upon inputting `0,1` into a field and the minValue is `0.2` to maxValue `1` it will accept the `0,1` due to float becoming `1` making the field accept the value, due to `1` being maxValue.\r\n\r\nIssue was initially reported on `discord.js` repo, but was informed it had nothing to do with them - but `discord` itself.\r\n\r\n[**OBS**: Ideas for fix posted in Comments, as a Regex Validator addition]\r\n\r\n### Steps to Reproduce\r\n\r\n1. Create SlashCommandBuilder\r\n2. Have the option `addNumberOption`\r\n3. Put in float values such as `.setMinValue(0.1)` & `.setMaxValue(1)`\r\n4. Notice when using the command the input `0,0.5` or `0,1` or `0,1.0` would be accepted due to commas being ignored by parseFloat values, as a result it would return `0.5` or `1` or `1.0` instead of blocking out if a comma is present.\r\n\r\n**Code Example**:\r\n```\r\n.addNumberOption((option) =>\r\n   option\r\n       .setName('growth')\r\n       .setDescription( 'Select Growth [0.1 - 1] • Remember a Decimal Point, if below growth 1. [Example: 0.45, 0.98, 1]')\r\n      .setRequired(true)\r\n      .setMinValue(0.1)\r\n      .setMaxValue(1)\r\n)\r\n                \r\n \r\nInside command:\r\n    console.log(growth) \r\n    Input: 0,1 => console.log(growth) => 1\r\n    Input: 0,1.0 => console.log(growth) => 1           \r\n```\r\n\r\n### Expected Behavior\r\n\r\nComma's in float values shouldn't be allowed, and thus the field should post \"error\" if thats the case, so a user cannot input `0,1` or `0,1.5` to get `1.5`\r\n\r\n**Expected Result(s):**\r\n`0,0.5 => Option error due to ,`\r\n`0.5 => Success`\r\n`0,1 => Option error due to ,`\r\n`1 => Success`\r\n`0.60 => Success`\r\n\r\n\r\n```\r\nInside command:\r\n    console.log(growth) \r\n    Input: 0,1 => Error: Not a valid critea (due to 0,)\r\n    Input: 0,1.0 => Error: Not a valid critea (due to 0,)\r\n    \r\n    Input 0.1 to 1 => Valid (as per minAmount & maxAmount)\r\n```\r\n\r\n### Current Behavior\r\n\r\n**Current Behaviour:**\r\n`0,0.5 => 0.5`\r\n`0,0.9 => 0.9`\r\n`0,1 => 1.0`\r\n`0,1.0 => 1`\r\n`1 => 1`\r\n\r\nAllowing `0,` in front of any float value, leading into stuff such as `0,1` becoming `1`  or `0,1.5` becoming `1.5`\r\n\r\n### Screenshots/Videos\r\n\r\n![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/17611705/233782866-65cc9c62-2d92-40dc-a5b9-4af82fef50b9.png)\r\n\r\n\r\n### Client and System Information\r\n\r\nDiscord: Stable 191606 (f870c7c) Host 1.0.9012 (31760) Windows 10 64-Bit (10.0.22621)\r\nUsing NodeJS & \"discord.js\": \"^14.9.1",
